--- !u!114 &6910906133244130492
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 6903722500528760356}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: dcdbb0b598fece24d9617cee6ae098e8, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  edit: 0
  note: "*** Agent Attack System \u2013 Hint ***\r\n\r\nWhat you need to know about
    this feature:\r\n\r\n- Random Attacks:\r\n  This agent can play random attack
    animations.\r\n  Set \"Max Attacks\" to any value greater than 1.\r\n  It will
    pick a random int between 1 and Max Attacks, \r\n  then trigger different animations
    on each attack.\r\n  Keep it at 1 to use only one animation.\r\n\r\n- How Attacks
    Work:\r\n  The agent will only attack if the target is inside the move range
    \r\n  (visible as the 3D orange gizmo).\r\n  It does not attack instantly \u2014
    it first chases the target, and \r\n  once the target touches the purple circle
    gizmo, \r\n  the attack behavior will start.\r\n\r\n- Applying Damage or Effects:\r\n 
    Brain script has an attack call type:\r\n    1. External: trigger via animation
    events or via script.\r\n    2. Automatic: trigger automatically on each call.\r\n 
    \r\n  This agent includes a method: ApplyAttack(int damage).\r\n  You can damage
    your target as you wish, no need to call it again, \r\n  since it's already invoked
    with a random damage value from \n  animation event or automatically.\r\n\r\n-
    Alert Noise:\r\n  Determines the radius (black wire sphere gizmo) in which other
    agents \r\n  will be immediately alerted when this agent first detects a target
    or make\n  make a sound by invoking CallAgents (location).\r\n  Increase this
    value to alarm nearby agents instantly.\r\n  Set it to 0 to disable the alert
    noise effect."
